{
  "requirement": "Validation MUST read the mdBook source directory from `[book].src` in `book.toml`, using `src` when the setting is absent. It MUST report an unreadable or malformed book configuration and reject an empty, absolute, or parent-traversing source path.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The behaviour is implemented and tested well, but the marking is incomplete. That is a gap under the criteria, so the judgment is false.\n\n**What is correct**\n- `book_source_dir` (src/evidence.rs ~l.200–253) reads `[book].src` from `book.toml` and defaults to `src` when `[book]` or `src` is absent.\n- It reports each of these cases:\n  - an unreadable `book.toml` (\"cannot read book configuration\"),\n  - invalid TOML,\n  - a non-table `book`,\n  - a non-string `book.src`.\n- It rejects an empty path, and any path with a component other than a normal one or `.`. That covers absolute paths, `..`, and Windows prefixes.\n- The unit test `book_source_defaults_only_when_absent_and_reports_invalid_configuration` (l.1310) covers these cases:\n  - the default when the file, `[book]`, or `src` is absent,\n  - an explicit `src`, including the inline-table form,\n  - a missing file,\n  - invalid TOML,\n  - a wrong type for `book` or `book.src` (int, bool, array, table),\n  - an empty path,\n  - an absolute path,\n  - `../outside`,\n  - `md/../outside`.\n- `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` also exercises the happy path through `validate_repository`.\n\n**Gap**\n- `inspect_repository_with_progress` (src/evidence.rs ~l.85–110) is the main validation entry point behind `validate_repository`. It calls `book_source_dir`, feeds the result into `collect_definitions`, and accumulates the errors.\n- It carries `{impl}` markers for many related requirements (`ci.errors`, `ci.diagnostics`, `configuration.loading`, and others). It has no `{impl}` for `requirements.ci.book_source`.\n- `load_definitions`, which makes the same call, does carry the marker. The marking is therefore inconsistent: part of the implementation, the validation path itself, lacks the reference.\n- No `FIXME` acknowledges this.\n\n**Minor points**\n- On any error the function returns `root.join(\"md\")` as a fallback source directory. The requirement does not specify this. It only keeps later discovery going after an error was recorded, but it is unspecified behaviour in the `{impl}` code.\n- No test checks that these errors surface through `validate_repository`. Only the helper is tested in isolation.",
